  "description": "This dataset contains near-infrared spectroscopy (NIRS) recordings from clinical monitoring sessions designed to evaluate motion artifact reduction techniques. The study implements collodion-fixed prism-based optical fibers to minimize motion-related noise in long-term NIRS monitoring, with applications to clinical neuroimaging and brain activity assessment. This dataset is mirrored on NEMAR from OpenNeuro (ds005929).",
  "methods_description": "Data were collected using NIRS with collodion-fixed prism-based optical fibers to reduce motion artifacts during clinical monitoring. The study was approved by the Massachusetts General Hospital Institutional Review Board.",
